(:case :src claude :form "(:read :file \"README.md\" :limit 5)" :want "(:read :file \"README.md\" :truncated true :limit 5 :maxBytes 12000 :totalLines 57 :more (:start 6 :end 57) :content \"# GenSEAM workspace\\n\\nLocal workspace for AgentSlang (ASL), the Addie agent and the packages around them. It has no git remote; `asl/` is published separately (see [`asl/README.md`](asl/README.md)).\\n\\nRationale: [MANIFESTO.md](MANIFESTO.md). Rules: `asl/grammar/rules.asn`, rendered into `CLAUDE.md` and `AGENTS.md`. Current architecture review: [`.asl/mem/tasks/SystemArchitectureReview.asn`](.asl/mem/tasks/SystemArchitectureReview.asn), with decisions and code navigation in [`.asl/mem/decisions/SystemArchitecture.asn`](.asl/mem/decisions/SystemArchitecture.asn); these are reviewed proposals, and measured capabilities are recorded separately in `asl/grammar/capabilities.asn`.\\n\")\n" :exit 0)
(:case :src claude :form "(:read :file \"README.md\" :start 1 :end 2)" :want "(:read :file \"README.md\" :start 1 :end 2 :content \"# GenSEAM workspace\\n\\n\")\n" :exit 0)
(:case :src claude :form "(:read :file \"README.md\")" :want "(:read :file \"README.md\" :content \"# GenSEAM workspace\\n\\nLocal workspace for AgentSlang (ASL), the Addie agent and the packages around them. It has no git remote; `asl/` is published separately (see [`asl/README.md`](asl/README.md)).\\n\\nRationale: [MANIFESTO.md](MANIFESTO.md). Rules: `asl/grammar/rules.asn`, rendered into `CLAUDE.md` and `AGENTS.md`. Current architecture review: [`.asl/mem/tasks/SystemArchitectureReview.asn`](.asl/mem/tasks/SystemArchitectureReview.asn), with decisions and code navigation in [`.asl/mem/decisions/SystemArchitecture.asn`](.asl/mem/decisions/SystemArchitecture.asn); these are reviewed proposals, and measured capabilities are recorded separately in `asl/grammar/capabilities.asn`.\\n\\n## What runs today\\n\\n- `bin/asl` is a bash and Python dispatcher over `bin/asl-core`, a prebuilt binary whose source is not in the tree. `asl check` and `asl test` run on asl-core, which is lenient: a file calling an unknown name passes `check`, and 0 counts as true.\\n- `asl/host/out/asl-host` (built by `asl/host/build.sh`) is the stage-0 C host and the strict reference: `asl-host check` resolves names, arity and enums, and `asl-host test` fails a suite whose assertions fail.\\n- `asl build` returns `ERR_UNIMPLEMENTED`; compiling ASL to C or WebAssembly is a target.\\n- The tree holds 1791 tracked `.asl` files and 240 tracked `.py` files (`git ls-files`, 2026-09-24).\\n\\n## Top-level packages\\n\\n| Path | Manifest description |\\n| :--- | :--- |\\n| [`asl/`](asl/) | The ASL language package: grammar, host, 46 packages under `asl/packages/` |\\n| [`agent/`](agent/) | Addie, the coding agent |\\n| [`agent-core/`](agent-core/) | Execution core, middleware pipeline and state machine |\\n| [`agent-bus/`](agent-bus/) | In-memory agent-to-agent communication mesh |\\n| [`harness/`](harness/) | Capability test harness and browser integration runner |\\n| [`code-intel/`](code-intel/) | Code intelligence graph, impact analysis, ASN navigator |\\n| [`mem/`](mem/) | Vector memory store and tiered context engine |\\n| [`crawler/`](crawler/) | Web crawler and in-browser automation |\\n\\n## Using the toolchain\\n\\nHuman plane, `./bin/asl <command>` (`./bin/asl help` lists them):\\n\\n```sh\\n./bin/asl check path/to/file.asl       # delimiter balance on asl-core\\n./bin/asl test path/to/fileTest.asl    # run a suite on asl-core\\nasl/host/out/asl-host test path/to/fileTest.asl   # strict run on the stage-0 host\\n./bin/asl intel outline path/to/file   # bounded outline; also impact, coupling, query\\n./bin/asl audit consistency            # balance, isolation, rules rendering, emoji\\n./bin/asl audit gates                  # the gate; --full runs every suite\\n```\\n\\nAgent plane, one or more ASN forms per call, run as one batch (`./bin/asl '(:tools)'` is the catalogue):\\n\\n```sh\\n./bin/asl '(:read :file \\\"README.md\\\" :limit 20)'\\n./bin/asl '(:query :text \\\"formatRagContext\\\")'\\n./bin/asl '(:edit :file \\\"path/to/file.asl\\\" :old \\\"x\\\" :new \\\"y\\\") (:diff)'   # stage, inspect\\n./bin/asl '(:flush)'                                          # or (:discard)\\n```\\n\\nRules and the agent skill are installed and checked with `./scripts/install.sh` (`--render-rules`, `--check-rules`, `--tier full`).\\n\\n## Gates\\n\\n`./bin/asl audit gates` runs the static checks (manifests, syntax, grounding against `asl/bench/publishedClaims.asn`, foreign-code allowlist and baseline, workspace isolation, grammar count, skills, rules, installer identity); `--full --sync` also runs every suite and compares failures with `.asl/mem/knownRed.asn`. `./bin/asl gate` prints a canned pass and is not a gate.\\n\\n## License\\n\\n`asl/` is dual-licensed under MIT or Apache-2.0 (`asl/LICENSE-MIT`, `asl/LICENSE-APACHE`). The workspace root carries no license file.\\n\")\n" :exit 0)
